{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363249-challenge-describe-your-character-using-only-three-details","id":1363249,"title":"CHALLENGE: Describe your character using only three details","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-24T21:30:56-08:00","id":1363249,"title":"CHALLENGE: Describe your character using only three details","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/pass-the-eyeliner\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.handbookofheroes.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/11/HH444.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/pass-the-eyeliner\" target=\"_blank\"> Pass the Eyeliner &ndash; The Handbook of Heroes </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/pass-the-eyeliner\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.handbookofheroes.com/archives/comic/pass-the-eyeliner </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T21:34:54-08:00","id":1363250,"title":"","content":"I don't follow blind links to sites I don't know. Can you explain in your own words?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-24T23:49:18-08:00","id":1363260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363249-challenge-describe-your-character-using-only-three-details?p=1363250#post1363250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't follow blind links to sites I don't know. Can you explain in your own words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the OP, but here\u2019s the blurb under the comic, which is what I\u2019m assuming they want us to explore\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s been a trip watching Laurel do sketch commissions at cons. I\u2019ll be standing there with my porkpie hat and cane trying to push the merch, but she\u2019ll be hunched over the table, busily busting out real-time art like she was a pizza place: Thirty minutes or less or it\u2019s on the house! But as impressive as it\u2019s been watching the art flow from her pen, it\u2019s the initial patron interviews that really stick with me.<br /> Laurel: \u201cSo what does your character look like? Hair? Eyes? Skin color? Distinguishing marks (scars, tattoos, glasses)? Style of hair? Hair color? General style? Are they fancy? Rugged? Primitive? Do they have some kind of motif? Ravens or roses on their armor? Anything like that?\u201d<br /> Meanwhile I\u2019ll be sitting there like, \u201cMy dude has scale mail and an axe.\u201d<br /> We\u2019ve already gone over some of territory in \u201cPortraiture,\u201d so I won\u2019t rehash any further. What I will say is that evil characters have an advantage in these conversations. That\u2019s for the simple reason that Evil is a theme you can work with. Sure there\u2019s a tradition of skulls and black leather, but that\u2019s just the outward manifestation of a greater truth. Evil is famous for its sense of style because it has style with a purpose.<br /> What I\u2019m saying is that, when you\u2019re a bad dude, you\u2019re crafting your look with intention. Maybe you\u2019re intimidating. Maybe you want your dude to be creepy, unsettling, or straight-up gross. But whichever brand of socially unacceptable you\u2019ve settled on, everything about the character design contributes to that impression. In the Evil Party, for example, Succubus is rocking that infernal red skin with the skimpy outfit of a temptress. She\u2019s also got the resting bitch face of a mean girl. Necromancer\u2019s outfit has a Disney-princess-gone-wrong vibe, with the inked-on tears to suggest her tragic romance with Paladin. Witch\u2019s oversize eyes are a nod towards her particular brand of crazy, and the hair is a throwback to the fairy tale terror of Japanese harionago. These are the things you\u2019ve got to think about when you\u2019re making a visual design.<br /> When you\u2019re working with a PC rather than a comic character, however, the temptation is to treat the character\u2019s appearance as a living record of your adventures. You\u2019re a complex, three-dimensional protagonist after all, and you want to convey the rich palette that is your dude. Therefore, rather than working towards a unifying motif, it\u2019s all too easy to transform your character into chronicle: She got this dagger from the first goblin she killed, and there\u2019s a bead from her dwarven foster father tied into her hair, and she has a scar on her throat from that time she got crit by a hag, and she bought these boots of speed last session. Now let me be clear: there\u2019s nothing inherently wrong with this kind of specificity. It can serve to make a character more fully of-the-world, and therefore help to increase your immersion into that world. But by the same token, when it comes time to describe your character in-game, this level of detail can overwhelm. For my money, what\u2019s more important by far is the overall impression. When you dude walks into a room, what\u2019s the first thing you notice? What kind of person are they?<br /> So for today\u2019s discussion, what do you say we try an exercise I learned back in undergrad? Describe your character using only three details. That\u2019s about how many items a reader can fit into their head after a first impression, and the same holds true in the oral landscape of the tabletop. If you choose wisely, we should get a coherent picture of your PC and their personality. I\u2019ll give you the usual race/class/gender stuff for free, so feel free to get specific with the other items. All clear on the \u2018three details\u2019 thing? OK then. Go! </div> </div> </div>(That said, I\u2019m with you, I\u2019d much rather have a premise explained to me rather than just left to intuit the OP\u2019s intention from a link.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T00:51:06-08:00","id":1363263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363249-challenge-describe-your-character-using-only-three-details?p=1363260#post1363260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not the OP, but here\u2019s the blurb under the comic, which is what I\u2019m assuming they want us to explore\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (That said, I\u2019m with you, I\u2019d much rather have a premise explained to me rather than just left to intuit the OP\u2019s intention from a link.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Sun be, that's a <b>lot</b> of words for what should have been a short paragraph or two of prompt by the OP. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-25T01:53:38-08:00","id":1363265,"title":"","content":"Brother Alazar, Zenith, monk of the Black Monastery of Leng;<br /> Coptic monk<br /> Slightly creepy vibe<br /> Missing left arm<br /> <br /> Dr Soma, Full Moon;<br /> Indian woman<br /> One eye<br /> Snake fangs<br /> <br /> I don't think this is that hard, but I think it's a bit reductive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/